    "answer": {
      "short": "$a,b,c$ are in geometric progression if and only if $\\frac ba=\\frac cb$, equivalently $b^2=ac$. Since $b>0$, this is equivalent to $b=\\sqrt{ac}$.",
      "worked": "If $a,b,c$ are in geometric progression, their consecutive ratios are equal:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac ba&=\\frac cb\\\\b^2&=ac\\\\b&=\\sqrt{ac}.\\end{align*}$$\nThe positive root is required because $b>0$.\n\nConversely, suppose $b=\\sqrt{ac}$. Then\n$$\\begin{align*}b^2&=ac\\\\\\frac ba&=\\frac cb.\\end{align*}$$\nDivision is valid because $a,b>0$. The consecutive ratios are equal, so $a,b,c$ are in geometric progression.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
